            <ArticleTitle>Serial angiographic evidence of rapid resolution of coronary artery stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>302-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An example of rapid, spontaneous resolution of an eccentric coronary luminal narrowing from 95 percent to 80 percent and subsequently to 50 percent stenosis over a six-week time period is presented. Spontaneous thrombolysis is proposed as the explanation for these changes and is discussed with reference to existing experimental and clinical observations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
